From: Stamp-P4 maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] esp32_sdio: raise RX workqueue and TX thread priority (#43)

Everything a Wi-Fi packet waits behind on the host runs at nice 0:
the RX workqueue and the esp_TX kthread each sit out a tick behind a
CPU-bound task.  On the board, running both at elevated priority
(rxprio=1 in the #43 debug build) roughly halved the worst P4-side TX
latency under flash-commit load (TX queue wait max 249 -> 126 ms,
sdio_claim_host() wait max 157 -> 66 ms).  SCHED_FIFO (rxprio=2) was
measurably worse - the FIFO threads starve each other around
sdio_claim_host() - so this stays inside CFS: WQ_HIGHPRI for
ESP_IF_RX_WORK_QUEUE and MIN_NICE for esp_TX, set once at start.

---
--- a/main.c
+++ b/main.c
@@ -1049,7 +1049,8 @@
 	memset(&adapter, 0, sizeof(adapter));
 
 	/* Prepare interface RX work */
-	adapter.if_rx_workqueue = alloc_workqueue("ESP_IF_RX_WORK_QUEUE", WQ_PERCPU, 0);
+	adapter.if_rx_workqueue = alloc_workqueue("ESP_IF_RX_WORK_QUEUE",
+						WQ_HIGHPRI | WQ_PERCPU, 0);
 
 	if (!adapter.if_rx_workqueue) {
 		deinit_adapter();
--- a/sdio/esp_sdio.c
+++ b/sdio/esp_sdio.c
@@ -1062,6 +1062,8 @@
 
 	context = adapter->if_context;
 
+	sched_set_normal(current, MIN_NICE);
+
 	while (!kthread_should_stop()) {
 
 		if (atomic_read(&context->adapter->state) < ESP_CONTEXT_READY) {
